From: OTA <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Makefile: build as gnu17

GCC 15 defaults to -std=gnu23, where bool, true and false are keywords,
and src/include/stddef.h defines them itself:

  src/include/stddef.h:18:15: error: 'bool' cannot be defined via 'typedef'
  src/include/stddef.h:19:8: error: cannot use keyword 'false' as enumeration constant

Pin the dialect the firmware was written for. Older compilers already
default to gnu17, so this changes nothing for them.

Upstream: N/A, project specific (applied after Buildroot's own patches)
---
 Makefile | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@ CFLAGS =-march=armv7-m -mcpu=cortex-m3 -mthumb -nostdlib -ffreestanding -Wall -W
 	-Werror-implicit-function-declaration -Wstrict-prototypes \
 	-Wdeclaration-after-statement -fno-delete-null-pointer-checks \
 	-Wempty-body -fno-strict-overflow -fno-stack-protector \
-	-fno-pie -fno-builtin -g -I$(INCLUDES) -O2 -MD
+	-fno-pie -fno-builtin -std=gnu17 -g -I$(INCLUDES) -O2 -MD
 LDFLAGS =-nostartfiles -fno-exceptions -Tfirmware.ld
 
 EXECUTABLE=am335x-pm-firmware.elf
